{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes","id":1523526,"title":"Hunger with \"changes\".","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-03T20:39:28-07:00","id":1523526,"title":"Hunger with \"changes\".","content":"This is something I'm testing and I wanted a second opinion, as beast hungers can be very uncomfortable I thought of these variants that might be more tolerable.<br /> <br /> Tyrants: Basically you can satisfy your hunger by exercising your authority or superiority. In the first case, the target needs to obey your command, but it needs to be something that she normally would not do willingly or does not like to do, whether due to laziness or pride. Superiority is highly explanatory, you would just have to prove that it is better in something whether physical or intellectual, however there are two important points in this case:<br /> <br /> 1. The victim in question must recognize defeat, so if he thinks the beast won by cheating, she won't receive satisfaction from the act;<br /> <br /> 2. The victim must be defeated at something that they value, even if they are not good at it.<br /> <br /> In the case of tyrants, the Beast feeds on the obedience or humiliation of the victim. Exercising your superiority over other beasts or other supernatural beings provides more satiety.<br /> <br /> Collectors: Collectors are treasure hunters, who satisfy their hunger by collecting precious things, however &quot;precious things&quot; have a very relative value depending on the family and the characteristics of each individual, Makaras tend to collect antiques, Ugallus collect compromising photos or evidence of crime, Anakim usually collect trophies from defeated opponents and so on. Detail, they only need to collect the object in question to satisfy themselves, what they do with it is at their discretion, however if the object already belongs to another person it cannot be given or purchased, it must be taken or at least obtained per bet, in some cases trade is a option.<br /> <br /> Predators: They are satisfied with the hunt, to satisfy their horrors they must track, ambush and capture/kill the prey, how much they are satisfied varies depending on how much the prey has been injured and how strong it is, other supernaturals usually grant a lot more satiety. They usually become hunters or if they live in cities, the healthiest option is to become hunters of offenders, like bounty hunters for example.<br /> <br /> Nemesis: Also known as bogeymen, they satisfy themselves by punishing bad children or bad adults, however they need to have committed a given crime or infraction to deserve the punishment, the beast must be sure that the given individual committed the infraction and the offender must know why he is being punished, otherwise he will not be able to be satisfied. Punishment can range from a scare to extreme damage to the body. The greater the crime, the greater the satisfaction.<br /> <br /> Ravager: Those who bring ruin, they are the simplest who are satisfied with destruction, but not just any destruction, the target needs to have some value either for the individual or for a community, if it is trash that no one cares about it won't have any effect. How much the destruction will satisfy the beast depends on the number and how much it will affect other people. In this case the beast is a change agent and it feeds from the victins emontions, be positive or negative.<br /> <br /> Along with this I would also put humanity points to balance and have a cost in case some beast goes overboard. In general terms it is very similar, in fact almost the same, I just put it in such a way that the Beasts need to sustain habits rather than feed on fears and traumas, although these would also be options.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T22:21:05-07:00","id":1523530,"title":"","content":"First... Beasts are monsters. What they do isn't supposed to be &quot;comfortable&quot; otherwise they wouldn't really be monsters. I don't see what the benefit of changing from &quot;feeding from fear,&quot; to &quot;feeding from habitual behaviors that result in fear and trauma,&quot; is supposed to accomplish. The only thing it can really do is let Beasts off easy. For example Collectors can just take whatever and it doesn't matter if their target cares about it. I can make a Namtaru that collects used chewing gum (which most people would find a revolting habit to have), but I don't need to worry about the person I'm taking the gum from, so I can just find a trash can near a school or something that I know kids that chew gum use a lot and loot it when nobody else is around.<br /> <br /> Second, adding more to track isn't a good thing. Beasts not having a &quot;morality&quot; track that says how good or bad they're being is a purposeful part of the game. Adding some sort of Humanity analog is both clunky design, and detracts from what's good about the game: Beasts decide who they are. Anything that creates objective right or wrong ways for Beasts to act is missing the point. Every Beast should be living in a state of tension where being pushed too hard could derail them from who they're trying to be; unless they've just given up and decided to be evil for the sake of evil and don't care anymore (which means you can pass them an Inheritance and move that character to NPC status if necessary). Beasts that go overboard already have to deal with either Satiety 0 or Satiety 10, which are nasty states to get stuck in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T22:54:05-07:00","id":1523533,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s been awhile since I delved into Beast, so I can\u2019t actually judge how much this differs from the official material as-is\u2026<br /> <br /> However, if the intention of the hack is to let Beasts subsist on \u2018lesser evils\u2019, I suggest making this a sort of alteration made to the original Beast template, rather than a full replacement/rewrite.<br /> Maybe it\u2019s the membership benefit of a Beastly cult. Maybe it\u2019s a state achieved by the possession of a magical item. Maybe it\u2019s something that just happens to Beasts that live in a specific area. Maybe it\u2019s the deceptively benign first-stage symptoms of a Contagion. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T01:02:16-07:00","id":1523536,"title":"","content":"Beasts in the RAW can generally get by just fine with a combination of low level feeding, and kinship to a supernatural type that's easy to make use of Family Dinner. The example low Satiety feedings are generally very easy to accomplish without making much of a fuss; you don't even really want to get a lot of Satiety out of them anyway, it's more to feed frequently enough for your Lair rating. Family Dinner can get you 1-3 Satiety as your main source of it just by watching another supernatural hunt and feed.<br /> <br /> There isn't a need to &quot;hack&quot; here to keep it to &quot;lesser&quot; evils. The tools are already in the game. A character that hungers for prey can make sure to spend their Satiety down to 3 before a weekly/twice weekly (for as powerful as most PCs are going to get with their Lairs) trip to hunt animals. Then bring your catch back to small church your changeling buddy helps run free meals for the homeless out of and you give your meat to. Soak up 2 Satiety from watching the changeling Harvest Glamour from the gratitude of those in need getting help making it through the week. So you're regularly be sitting around 5-6 Satiety to do actual major scenes and you can then get that back down to 3 to rinse and repeat.<br /> <br /> Obviously a serious story is going to upset such routines in some fashion to add some challenge to the PC's life, but the bar for &quot;lesser evil&quot; in the books is so low any hack trying to lower it seems pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T06:33:02-07:00","id":1523547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523530#post1523530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First... Beasts are monsters. What they do isn't supposed to be &quot;comfortable&quot; otherwise they wouldn't really be monsters. I don't see what the benefit of changing from &quot;feeding from fear,&quot; to &quot;feeding from habitual behaviors that result in fear and trauma,&quot; is supposed to accomplish. The only thing it can really do is let Beasts off easy. For example Collectors can just take whatever and it doesn't matter if their target cares about it. I can make a Namtaru that collects used chewing gum (which most people would find a revolting habit to have), but I don't need to worry about the person I'm taking the gum from, so I can just find a trash can near a school or something that I know kids that chew gum use a lot and loot it when nobody else is around.<br /> <br /> Second, adding more to track isn't a good thing. Beasts not having a &quot;morality&quot; track that says how good or bad they're being is a purposeful part of the game. Adding some sort of Humanity analog is both clunky design, and detracts from what's good about the game: Beasts decide who they are. Anything that creates objective right or wrong ways for Beasts to act is missing the point. Every Beast should be living in a state of tension where being pushed too hard could derail them from who they're trying to be; unless they've just given up and decided to be evil for the sake of evil and don't care anymore (which means you can pass them an Inheritance and move that character to NPC status if necessary). Beasts that go overboard already have to deal with either Satiety 0 or Satiety 10, which are nasty states to get stuck in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you have any suggetions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T11:29:18-07:00","id":1523565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523530#post1523530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First... Beasts are monsters. What they do isn't supposed to be &quot;comfortable&quot; otherwise they wouldn't really be monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can play a Forsaken without being uncomfortable. I can play a Kindred without being uncomfortable. The players being uncomfortable playing their characters is a problem, characters in game being uncomfortable is different. I think this is rewritten for the first case. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see what the benefit of changing from &quot;feeding from fear,&quot; to &quot;feeding from habitual behaviors that result in fear and trauma,&quot; is supposed to accomplish. The only thing it can really do is let Beasts off easy. For example Collectors can just take whatever and it doesn't matter if their target cares about it. I can make a Namtaru that collects used chewing gum (which most people would find a revolting habit to have), but I don't need to worry about the person I'm taking the gum from, so I can just find a trash can near a school or something that I know kids that chew gum use a lot and loot it when nobody else is around. </div> </div> </div>Now I'm imagining a beast that's all the horrible halloween stories we were told as children, drugs in bubble gum, razor blades in candy bars...<br /> <br /> That said your example is EXTREMELY flawed. OP said &quot;precious things&quot; and you're having them take trash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T12:40:42-07:00","id":1523568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523536#post1523536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts in the RAW can generally get by just fine with a combination of low level feeding, and kinship to a supernatural type that's easy to make use of Family Dinner. The example low Satiety feedings are generally very easy to accomplish without making much of a fuss; you don't even really want to get a lot of Satiety out of them anyway, it's more to feed frequently enough for your Lair rating. Family Dinner can get you 1-3 Satiety as your main source of it just by watching another supernatural hunt and feed.<br /> <br /> There isn't a need to &quot;hack&quot; here to keep it to &quot;lesser&quot; evils. The tools are already in the game. A character that hungers for prey can make sure to spend their Satiety down to 3 before a weekly/twice weekly (for as powerful as most PCs are going to get with their Lairs) trip to hunt animals. Then bring your catch back to small church your changeling buddy helps run free meals for the homeless out of and you give your meat to. Soak up 2 Satiety from watching the changeling Harvest Glamour from the gratitude of those in need getting help making it through the week. So you're regularly be sitting around 5-6 Satiety to do actual major scenes and you can then get that back down to 3 to rinse and repeat.<br /> <br /> Obviously a serious story is going to upset such routines in some fashion to add some challenge to the PC's life, but the bar for &quot;lesser evil&quot; in the books is so low any hack trying to lower it seems pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that, you know that and I think the majority here thinks similarly, however the fact is that this isn't a consensus and that is what I want to touch on, to imagine the game being more tolerable, I don't even know if that word is the right one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T13:33:14-07:00","id":1523570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523547#post1523547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, you have any suggetions?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523568#post1523568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that, you know that and I think the majority here thinks similarly, however the fact is that this isn't a consensus and that is what I want to touch on, to imagine the game being more tolerable, I don't even know if that word is the right one.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> It's hard to make suggestions when I don't really know what you want. You can't house rules your way out of people not knowing what the game actually allows and what the rules actually are. You're not going to convince all the BtP haters out there to give the game a shot by changing a few words in how feeding is framed or adding a Humanity meter.<br /> <br /> If you have a potential group of people that might want to play it, but are unsure, just address the development failures of the core book, acknowledge the tonal problems, and commit to running the game according to its potential instead of being beholden to some poorly worded passages. If that's not good enough, it's probably doomed to failure unless you plan on doing a full fan rewrite of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523565#post1523565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The players being uncomfortable playing their characters is a problem, characters in game being uncomfortable is different. I think this is rewritten for the first case.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. But without know what part of it makes them uncomfortable it' hard to know what to actually say. Is this discomfort based on a quick skim of the text that missed important nuances? It is based on all the negative online bashing of the game that doesn't care how accurate it is to the text? It is based on a bad experience with a ST already? Is it just Beast's purposeful choice to not put a fantasy layer between Beasts and the harm they do unlike other CofD supernaturals?<br /> <br /> All of those are different issues with different solutions. Though none of them are really addressed in the OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I'm imagining a beast that's all the horrible halloween stories we were told as children, drugs in bubble gum, razor blades in candy bars... </div> </div> </div>OK? Though it really wouldn't do a Beast much good to indulge in such things on a regular basis. It might be good for working on their Legend or trying to create some potential Chambers, but it's not really a functional feeding strategy to sate their Hunger.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, some of these sorts of moral panic urban legends are also a potential reaction to a Beast that uses certain Nightmares too frequently that people start actually thinking dream-threats are real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said your example is EXTREMELY flawed. OP said &quot;precious things&quot; and you're having them take trash. </div> </div> </div>Not really, because unlike your attempted counter, I didn't stop reading at those two word and took the whole Collector section into account. The section concedes that &quot;precious&quot; is highly subjective, and that Family should be the guide for what is precious to the Beast in question. Namtaru are the fear of revolting things. Trash, especially trash associating with used food and bodily fluids, is naturally repellent to most humans, and thus has value (aka is &quot;precious&quot;) to that Family. A Namtaru Collector's collection should be disgusting, and for that purpose, trash is treasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-04-2023, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T16:10:25-07:00","id":1523580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523570#post1523570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> It's hard to make suggestions when I don't really know what you want. You can't house rules your way out of people not knowing what the game actually allows and what the rules actually are. You're not going to convince all the BtP haters out there to give the game a shot by changing a few words in how feeding is framed or adding a Humanity meter.<br /> <br /> If you have a potential group of people that might want to play it, but are unsure, just address the development failures of the core book, acknowledge the tonal problems, and commit to running the game according to its potential instead of being beholden to some poorly worded passages. If that's not good enough, it's probably doomed to failure unless you plan on doing a full fan rewrite of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I wouldn't even try, the way things are today, at best, I would have a polite refusal, at worst, no mention. My interest in this sensitive point is more of a personal project and not related to a group, even though an opinion like this could be useful. Let's face it, a Beast fan game would be very difficult, even unnecessary, without changing their entire concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523570#post1523570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bNot really, because unlike your attempted counter, I didn't stop reading at those two word and took the whole Collector section into account. The section concedes that &quot;precious&quot; is highly subjective, and that Family should be the guide for what is precious to the Beast in question. Namtaru are the fear of revolting things. Trash, especially trash associating with used food and bodily fluids, is naturally repellent to most humans, and thus has value (aka is &quot;precious&quot;) to that Family. A Namtaru Collector's collection should be disgusting, and for that purpose, trash is treasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nantaru have the concept of repulsion, but they are not just that, they are also linked to the dualities of ugly and beautiful, weak and strong, poor and rich, smaller and bigger, basically how one oppresses the other, it was this concept that I wanted to use it, having said that in their case it wouldn't be what you take, but who you take it from. I certainly should have explained this part, but I thought this was a concept that was already known, the gorgons give off a nosferatu vibe, at least to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T17:19:26-07:00","id":1523583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523580#post1523580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interest in this sensitive point is more of a personal project and not related to a group,...</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the goal of the project?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's face it, a Beast fan game would be very difficult, even unnecessary, without changing their entire concept. </div> </div> </div>The number of us still hoping that Arc finally works up the time and energy to do one doesn't really mesh with this assessment.<br /> <br /> As well, there's a freedom to fan work. Onyx Path made it very clear they didn't want to take on the effort of doing Kindred of the East 20th Anniversary, because balance the need to fix all the bad with doing honor to the &quot;Anniversary&quot; aspect wasn't something they wanted to attempt. Fans have since put out an excellent KotE20 book. It might not fix enough for some people, or stick close enough to the original for others, but as fans they didn't have to worry about those cases. Esp. with someone like Arc being interested in making something like that happen for Beast, it's a lot more realistic than I think you're giving credit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T20:34:06-07:00","id":1523589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523583#post1523583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the goal of the project?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The number of us still hoping that Arc finally works up the time and energy to do one doesn't really mesh with this assessment.<br /> <br /> As well, there's a freedom to fan work. Onyx Path made it very clear they didn't want to take on the effort of doing Kindred of the East 20th Anniversary, because balance the need to fix all the bad with doing honor to the &quot;Anniversary&quot; aspect wasn't something they wanted to attempt. Fans have since put out an excellent KotE20 book. It might not fix enough for some people, or stick close enough to the original for others, but as fans they didn't have to worry about those cases. Esp. with someone like Arc being interested in making something like that happen for Beast, it's a lot more realistic than I think you're giving credit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't referring to a system, but in Lore itself, Beast's content seems more like a complement than something that weighs within the world of darkness. The Dark Mother doesn't seem to matter so much at the end of the day, being an abstract figure and alien to the rest and Still, the game seems to work, I suppose it's on purpose to give freedom, that being said, I believe it would need a change, but If you have any success, let me know.<br /> <br /> As for my project, it's not even a real project. I just saw the old WOD and saw concepts that COD presented and... I think you get the idea, basically it's a fool's quest, do they use that term in the USA?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T20:49:13-07:00","id":1523591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523589#post1523589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't referring to a system, but in Lore itself, Beast's content seems more like a complement than something that weighs within the world of darkness. The Dark Mother doesn't seem to matter so much at the end of the day, being an abstract figure and alien to the rest</div> </div> </div> </div>She is, by direct comparison, at least an Aeon-equivalent Astral being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> basically it's a fool's quest, do they use that term in the USA?\u200b </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fool's errand&quot; is a known-enough expression in American English, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T21:27:40-07:00","id":1523593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523591#post1523591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is, by direct comparison, at least an Aeon-equivalent Astral being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Aeon isn't a strictly widely understood term outside of context, the context:<br /> <br /> Aeons are the [Phenomenal/Fallen] Astral* God/Representatives of ten fundamental forces/aspects of reality that the Awakened Mages call the Arcana, so effectively within that confine each is a 1 in 10 ruler of the experiential reality-within the confines of understanding reality <i>as</i> those 10 forces/aspects.<br /> <br /> The Progenitor-Beasts, the various spouses of the Dark Mother, are being ascribed to that same sort of tier of power and rulership/representation of/over reality. The Dark Mother is a locus of their attention and connection, and is at least on par with them, or possibly <i>above </i>them(Beasts and other adjacent's define the realm of soulscapes that identifies the <i>world's</i> soulscape as The Mother's Land, which if hyperbole probably isn't hard earned hyperbole all the same, and there's a lot of hay to be made over how it's <i>not</i> hyperbole).<br /> <br /> All of this is kind of semantic, and some it is definitely the realm of academic debate for nerds in the games, but the short hand-all of these people/things/ideas are at the top of the hierarchy of the Astral Realms, and quite possibly some of the highest acting actors in the Ephemeral Entities food chain on the whole.<br /> <br /> But what is pertinent is....<i>she's actually quite active in the lives of Beasts</i> (and other monsters, if I ever fucking finish this &quot;The Dreaming and the Dark Mother in the lives of other splats without Beasts, Heroes, or Insatiable&quot; supplement outline). She's not abstract and alien, she's <i>very disturbingly present</i>.<br /> <br /> *since it's been implied for this to be coming from a World of Darkness perspective**, Imagine the High Umbra as it's own realm, but with less bullshit.<br /> **although if you are coming from World of Darkness, <i>seriously</i>? You need to tone <i>Beast's Hunger</i> down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-05-2023, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T23:03:08-07:00","id":1523603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523589#post1523589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it would need a change, but If you have any success, let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've run two games, and played in three games of BtP or mixed group CofD. While everyone involved would appreciate a &quot;1.5&quot; edition of the game, we did just fine with the core book and existing supplements. Most of our homebrew was in things like Kinship Merits and Nightmares since you're supposed to come up with more of those than the examples in the books. We found very little need to change the game's content: lore or mechanics.<br /> <br /> There's definitely rough spots where the books could be better (hence the desire for a 1.5 edition made by freelancer writers operating as fans), but the biggest problems I've had with the game are people not being interested in it at all (often vehemently), not problems with running the game once I find people up for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you get the idea, basically it's a fool's quest, do they use that term in the USA?\u200b </div> </div> </div>While, as noted, the phrase is used in American English too, I'm not sure I get &quot;the idea.&quot; You might be aiming for something you acknowledge isn't possible to achieve, but I still don't know what you're aiming for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T07:23:32-07:00","id":1523630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523593#post1523593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Aeon isn't a strictly widely understood term outside of context, the context:<br /> <br /> Aeons are the [Phenomenal/Fallen] Astral* God/Representatives of ten fundamental forces/aspects of reality that the Awakened Mages call the Arcana, so effectively within that confine each is a 1 in 10 ruler of the experiential reality-within the confines of understanding reality <i>as</i> those 10 forces/aspects.<br /> <br /> The Progenitor-Beasts, the various spouses of the Dark Mother, are being ascribed to that same sort of tier of power and rulership/representation of/over reality. The Dark Mother is a locus of their attention and connection, and is at least on par with them, or possibly <i>above </i>them(Beasts and other adjacent's define the realm of soulscapes that identifies the <i>world's</i> soulscape as The Mother's Land, which if hyperbole probably isn't hard earned hyperbole all the same, and there's a lot of hay to be made over how it's <i>not</i> hyperbole).<br /> <br /> All of this is kind of semantic, and some it is definitely the realm of academic debate for nerds in the games, but the short hand-all of these people/things/ideas are at the top of the hierarchy of the Astral Realms, and quite possibly some of the highest acting actors in the Ephemeral Entities food chain on the whole.<br /> <br /> But what is pertinent is....<i>she's actually quite active in the lives of Beasts</i> (and other monsters, if I ever fucking finish this &quot;The Dreaming and the Dark Mother in the lives of other splats without Beasts, Heroes, or Insatiable&quot; supplement outline). She's not abstract and alien, she's <i>very disturbingly present</i>.<br /> <br /> *since it's been implied for this to be coming from a World of Darkness perspective**, Imagine the High Umbra as it's own realm, but with less bullshit.<br /> **although if you are coming from World of Darkness, <i>seriously</i>? You need to tone <i>Beast's Hunger</i> down?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, about reducing the tone, I don't have a problem, but I think you know the bad reputation that BTP received, there are people who hate this title like hell, excume me the expression. That said, I wanted to give it a try.<br /> <br /> Second, apart from choosing the beasts, and perhaps the heroes, at the end of the day the Dark Mother, I'll call her Tiamat, doesn't really do that much, as far as I've seen at least, she doesn't interfere or plan to interfere with the world directly, it also doesn't have a cult or organization doing something for her or because of her, or someone researching about her. The book treats her more as an untouchable causer like the triad of the old WOD, but without everything that is created around it, except the insatiable, I like their concept, it's like they are a cancer.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T07:38:30-07:00","id":1523631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523603#post1523603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've run two games, and played in three games of BtP or mixed group CofD. While everyone involved would appreciate a &quot;1.5&quot; edition of the game, we did just fine with the core book and existing supplements. Most of our homebrew was in things like Kinship Merits and Nightmares since you're supposed to come up with more of those than the examples in the books. We found very little need to change the game's content: lore or mechanics.<br /> <br /> There's definitely rough spots where the books could be better (hence the desire for a 1.5 edition made by freelancer writers operating as fans), but the biggest problems I've had with the game are people not being interested in it at all (often vehemently), not problems with running the game once I find people up for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While, as noted, the phrase is used in American English too, I'm not sure I get &quot;the idea.&quot; You might be aiming for something you acknowledge isn't possible to achieve, but I still don't know what you're aiming for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically I saw concepts that I liked in CofD and, concepts that I like, and I think about how to adapt them, or if I should, for the old WoD, you or someone you know must have done something similar, if not in this, in another game, It would be the same thing, but on a larger scale. By the way, I'm not promising anything, it's just a personal project so I might just lose interest and that's it, but anyway, I think you understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T09:46:19-07:00","id":1523642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523630#post1523630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, about reducing the tone, I don't have a problem, but I think you know the bad reputation that BTP received, there are people who hate this title like hell, excume me the expression. That said, I wanted to give it a try.<br /> <br /> Second, apart from choosing the beasts, and perhaps the heroes, at the end of the day the Dark Mother, I'll call her Tiamat, doesn't really do that much, as far as I've seen at least, she doesn't interfere or plan to interfere with the world directly, it also doesn't have a cult or organization doing something for her or because of her, or someone researching about her. The book treats her more as an untouchable causer like the triad of the old WOD, but without everything that is created around it, except the insatiable, I like their concept, it's like they are a cancer.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I didn't say a thing about that, say it to someone who did.<br /> <br /> Second, I'm not sure how much you've read of the line or how much familiarity you have with Chronicles cosmology and metaphysics, but the thing of the matter is that it's actually hard to imagine the Dark Mother (I will not be calling her Tiamat because I don't see any value in doing so, and I think it's weird others do) actually just confining her business to Beasts. For starters, she's actually really active with Beasts in a way that other entities of her scale aren't. It's her power that's being used whenever Beasts call upon Obcasus Rites, and there are circumstances where she offers direct guidance (and correspondingly power via Willpower) to Beasts, a thing that even the Judges, as one of her most direct competitors in interaction, doesn't do. Next, as the psychospiritual goddess-symbol of monstrosity itself, she has a sympathetic connection towards pretty much everything else in the world of Chronicles, and it becomes weird to consider her involvement with Beasts and think she arbitrarily stops there, particularly since there are touches throughout the gameline that really suggest otherwise. Finally, there are plenty of points in other splats where it's not terribly hard to understand The Dark Mother's involvement.<br /> <br /> Arguably, the main reason we don't have elaboration on that is just simply that Beast never got a book that allowed them to discuss the idea-the Core book has to establish the basics of the world, Building the Legend is centered on setting and chronicle building, Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes was about developing opposition, and the Beast's Player Guide was about increasing the toolbox for players. Since we never got a Storyteller's Guide, we never got a chance to have a dedicated look at the Dark Mother and what she does and can do in a chronicle, including games that don't include Beasts, Heroes, or Insatiable.<br /> <br /> She's a designated figure in a game dedicated to a crossover-centric splat. It's hard to imagine that she doesn't crossover.<br /> <br /> And your willingness to use cancer as a metaphor doesn't do much to inspire confidence in your handling of Beast and it's concepts, <i>now</i> I am commenting on your tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T13:18:14-07:00","id":1523656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523631#post1523631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically I saw concepts that I liked in CofD and, concepts that I like, and I think about how to adapt them, or if I should, for the old WoD,...</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a thread about this in the spring, we both posed in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T14:50:44-07:00","id":1523665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523642#post1523642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, I didn't say a thing about that, say it to someone who did.<br /> <br /> Second, I'm not sure how much you've read of the line or how much familiarity you have with Chronicles cosmology and metaphysics, but the thing of the matter is that it's actually hard to imagine the Dark Mother (I will not be calling her Tiamat because I don't see any value in doing so, and I think it's weird others do) actually just confining her business to Beasts. For starters, she's actually really active with Beasts in a way that other entities of her scale aren't. It's her power that's being used whenever Beasts call upon Obcasus Rites, and there are circumstances where she offers direct guidance (and correspondingly power via Willpower) to Beasts, a thing that even the Judges, as one of her most direct competitors in interaction, doesn't do. Next, as the psychospiritual goddess-symbol of monstrosity itself, she has a sympathetic connection towards pretty much everything else in the world of Chronicles, and it becomes weird to consider her involvement with Beasts and think she arbitrarily stops there, particularly since there are touches throughout the gameline that really suggest otherwise. Finally, there are plenty of points in other splats where it's not terribly hard to understand The Dark Mother's involvement.<br /> <br /> Arguably, the main reason we don't have elaboration on that is just simply that Beast never got a book that allowed them to discuss the idea-the Core book has to establish the basics of the world, Building the Legend is centered on setting and chronicle building, Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes was about developing opposition, and the Beast's Player Guide was about increasing the toolbox for players. Since we never got a Storyteller's Guide, we never got a chance to have a dedicated look at the Dark Mother and what she does and can do in a chronicle, including games that don't include Beasts, Heroes, or Insatiable.<br /> <br /> She's a designated figure in a game dedicated to a crossover-centric splat. It's hard to imagine that she doesn't crossover.<br /> <br /> And your willingness to use cancer as a metaphor doesn't do much to inspire confidence in your handling of Beast and it's concepts, <i>now</i> I am commenting on your tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something wrong in compare with cancer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T14:51:50-07:00","id":1523666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523656#post1523656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was a thread about this in the spring, we both posed in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember this one, but in that case was just about BtP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T15:32:51-07:00","id":1523668,"title":"","content":"Well, since I'm in it now, let's address a few things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523630#post1523630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but I think you know the bad reputation that BTP received, there are people who hate this title like hell, excume me the expression. .\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I am quite aware of it, thank you. And here's my response:<br /> <br /> So?<br /> <br /> Lots of people hated Chronicles when it was created, but it clearly didn't become what it is now by listening to those people. Lots of people thought Requiem was the worst thing to have ever been created, does that mean that Rose Bailey should have made Requiem to the request of those haters? Lots of people hated that Curse had their characters come from a fixed location and were basically ensured to be non-white characters, does that mean C.A. Sulieman should have instead defocused and watered down Curse just so people could have their Mayan mummies? Lots of people hated the tech in techgnostic espionage for Descent, does that mean that Rose Bailey should have weakened her unique take and laid out another fucking boring Christian-inspired take?<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: people who hate things aren't equipped to provide good direction on how to improve a work by virtue of hating the thing. We've seen a lot of takes on how to &quot;improve&quot; Beast over the years, and to be quite frank, every single one that came in from someone who hated the game and had a cocksure answer for how to fix have quite frankly been worse ideas, from having terrible mechanical operations to being incredibly boring. These people, motivated by heightened emotion and arrogance, often just act instead of taking the time to really dig into and gain an understanding of what <i>actually</i> needs working, and instead just chase after fixes that are superficially shiny but substantially anemic.<br /> <br /> And in the end, what does trying to appeal to people who hate the game do? Realistically, they're still gonna hate the game, just because it <i>is</i>. The nature of the argument might change, but honestly there will always be something they can grab as a reason to hate it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Beast <i>has</i> an audience, it <i>has</i> a fanbase. These are people who can see and appreciate the flaws and the way those problems work, but they can also hone in on what works about it to, and can reemphasize those point and build from them to strengthen the game all the better, and from there glean answers to solve those problems. Why the fuck would I want to appeal to haters when I can take greater insight from the people who actually care about the game and use that to create a strong base of evangelism for the game?<br /> <br /> If it was possible to turn around opinion on Beast, it's not by catering to the whims and conceits of it's haters-it's simply by working to make Beast a better game, by making it the best version of itself.<br /> <br /> All of this is moot, because with Paradox doing what they're doing, even if we released the most stellar stealth 1.5 version of Beast ever, the lack of promotion means that for most people, Beast is going to forever and always be that game that blows monkey chunks. So, again, why bother appealing to them when I can write for the fanbase that exists? Anyone who wants to give it a chance can easily find it.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I can gain insight from the haters, but design the game for them? That's just a waste of everybody's time. <hr />Going on the subject of Hunger, the actual problems that stand with it is that it's easy to have normal Satiation be overshadowed by employment with Family Dinner. Part of this problem is that there's not enough demonstration on what can be done for Hungers (which also addresses the things people get squeamish about) and in being clear about high Satiation being the premise of story (-arcs). There's a couple of ways you can actually deal with the problem, mostly down presentation-having the Hunger sections actually get into what's going and can be done with them is a big one (I have a format floating on my drive that I reckon handily covers some of the differentiation, examining Hunger through the lens of To Take and Destroy [since the universal is to strip away the security devices, and the natural followup is to remove it forever], To Keep and Build [because Beasts have their own ambitions and ideals, their satiations acting as stepping stones for them], and To Return and Gift [because once the Satiation is done, a Beast doesn't have to keep their victims suffering from the loss-a decently connected Predator can even restore health and wholeness-and they can also take the subjects of their Satiations and bestow them to people who they find deserving of it), you can discuss Satiation in the storytelling section and provide examples of how to build stories around Hunger throughout the book, maybe even incorporate a subsystem if you feel insecure about it, and you can even build in reasons for intentionality to Satiation into mechanics-the Forswearing mechanic for my take on Heroes is rooted in providing incentives for Beasts to find ways to have their Satiation provide catharsis for the victims, as examples-you can re-emphasize that monsters can also be the subject of Satiation, and you could also just straight up have incentives built into Satiating Hunger (I made a pitch for something like that when the BPG was beginning development, and it was the only idea that didn't make it into the book, so there may be flaws with that idea, but still).<br /> <br /> Chronicles very frequently has players commit to the sort of actions that make up Hungers. Beast's problem on the subject is not that Hungers are harsh as they are, or even as real as they are, it's that there wasn't enough focus on what can be done with it and about it.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523565#post1523565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can play a Forsaken without being uncomfortable. I can play a Kindred without being uncomfortable. The players being uncomfortable playing their characters is a problem, characters in game being uncomfortable is different. I think this is rewritten for the first case.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this hits on something kind of important, because my instant reaction reading this first time was &quot;I would probably chalk that up to either you screwing up or your Storyteller screwing up.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's rude on my part, and more importantly limited (I'll get to that in a second), but on the anecdotal side of things, I <i>have</i> been uncomfortable playing a werewolf and a vampire (dear lord, have I been disturbed by playing a vampire). From one perspective, these characters are monsters, and what they do to get by is unnerving-that's the point of personal horror. I've made choices in regards to the execution of violence as an Uratha that made me stare in horror at the consequences. I've had characters strip human people to the bone of their free will and agency because it was convenient for my vampire, and it was deeply unsettling.<br /> <br /> But, like, if I stuck to that as my response, I would also be a hypocrite (and very particularly, in a way I would actually have a problem with), because I've also had slice-of-life games of Requiem where the biggest threat was we lost the Prince's dog and had to scramble to find the little scamp before the night was up. I've had games of Mage where we've &quot;infiltrated&quot; a Mormon temple and had one player have a nightmare by getting caught up in doing their ritual of baptisms for the dead because they just plain sucked at social scenarios. I've had games of Hunter where an extended sequence was almost like something out of Scooby Doo as a paranoid player was getting jerked around by spooky seeming but harmless elements of the scene.<br /> <br /> Players have a latitutde that game designers often don't, because you can play the game how you want, but game designers usually need to have and keep to a strong design focus to make their products snap. Players can play Chronicles as a horror game, an urban fantasy, a slice of life iyashikei, action-comedy, or what have you, and I've seen it be done.<br /> <br /> But games don't always have that flexibility, and no game can be for all people. Going out of house for a second, Bluebeard's Bride is a pretty tightly designed game focused on feminine horror and doesn't have a lot of latitude for doing anything but that. There are a lot of people who don't like or can't play Bluebeard's Bride because it's horror hits really close to home for them. There are also a lot of people who love the game because it does <i>exactly that</i>. That it hits so close on intimately painful topics is not a reason to not buy Bluebeard's Bride, it just means that it's not for everyone.<br /> <br /> Beast could have definitely benefited from dedicated sensitivity readers and having a developer who could actually pay attention when their writer's raise concerns about the material instead of juggling, like, four or five development projects on top of their day job, but suggesting that Tyrants feeding by popping someone's arm out of it's socket is too much when I've been unnerved by my Storyteller's making clear the pain and loss of power a NPC is feeling when my Cahalith popped their arm out of their socket is nonsensical. It IS important to understand that that makes it not a game that's going to be for everyone (I've frequently made the point that even a well-made Beast is probably a niche product), and it IS important to be mindful about how subjects are discussed-handling the mental health and wellbeing of readers and players is a paramount subject for any horror game-but it's <i>also</i> important to remember that some people pick up a game about personal horror expecting to experience some amount of personal horror, and while the execution of Hungers is very flawed, it's base idea sits soundly in that place.<br /> <br /> Not everyone is going be comfortable with the fact that Beasts don't have a fictional sheen over their violence. A lot of people find it very par for the course with Chronicles of Darkness. Both are fine reactions to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T15:35:11-07:00","id":1523669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523665#post1523665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something wrong in compare with cancer?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a very revealing word choice regarding your intentions for this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T18:26:19-07:00","id":1523672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1523669#post1523669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a very revealing word choice regarding your intentions for this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only compared the Insatiables to a cancer because they simply feel hungry, they are always hungry and unlike the Beasts, which seem to work in harmony with the primordial dream, as strange as it may sound, the fears that the Insatiables devour don't return to the primoridal dream, so they consume resources without giving anything in return and that's also taking into account that they hunt beasts to feed on, which in theory are healthy cells, and take their Lairs, that being said, compare them to cancer, which is something that's kind of that devours you from the inside, seems palpable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T17:47:51-07:00","id":1524666,"title":"","content":"This will seem strange, but what would you think if BTP's theme was about ambition? I mean, in this case the horrors are monsters that despite being nightmares are attracted by the ambition of their human part, whether this ambition is repressed or not, in this case they are very extreme desires, it would be in this game of balance between the morality of the human part or unbridled desire for horror. Does it seem too forced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T18:21:06-07:00","id":1524667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1524666#post1524666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will seem strange, but what would you think if BTP's theme was about ambition? I mean, in this case the horrors are monsters that despite being nightmares are attracted by the ambition of their human part, whether this ambition is repressed or not, in this case they are very extreme desires, it would be in this game of balance between the morality of the human part or unbridled desire for horror. Does it seem too forced?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said before, that in the reductive way to think of games way of analogizing them to singular aspects of human life, the same way some people will say Created is a game about childhood and Curse is a game about old age, that Beast would pretty clearly be the game about celebrity, that they are myth and folklore and creepy pasta given flesh, heart and mind, that it's a game about becoming memetic in that way that haunted houses and death turns and hurricanes and earthquakes do, monstrosity gone viral, and I have taken that read so far as to say that my personal theme for Beast on the whole is <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZDXXi19_7iE\" target=\"_blank\">The Monster by Eminem</a>, so no, I wouldn't say it's <i>too</i> forced.<br /> <br /> That said, Beast is, in a game about monsters, is a crossover template, and by way of being able to relate to any and all of the other splats, ended up in a place where it must reflect and contrast them, and has opted for the route of deconstruction, acting as a mirror that strips the circumstances that makes other monsters defensible (to be crass about it, strips the bullshit from the subject) and shows who they are and what they do in raw terms-a useful if uncomfortable role to play in pairing with any other sort of character.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem for Beasts that comes with that is that, by also scraping all the circumstance that makes other monsters defensible, not having all the reasons that it's <i>not</i> <i>their fault</i> they're like that, is that it means each and every Beast is personally accountable for what they do with their Hunger-it's on <i>them</i> for whatever they do. They don't get to blame the Curses or Luna or their Obsessions or Torment or the Strangers or their Geist or the Judges or the God-Machine or the Conspiracies, or even monstrosity itself, for what they do. And because of that, it's on them to put in the time, energy, effort, and thought in just what they are going to bend their Hunger toward, who they will be in the community and why that will be the case-and how they'll sustain it against extensive scrutiny.<br /> <br /> After all, for every haunted house left to stand, there are just as many that get bulldozed and paved over.<br /> <br /> Celebrity, ambition-these are words for social accountability, at the end of the day-these are words that describe <i>character</i>, in a game that has the other half of it's makeup in a form of storytelling notorious for it's maxim of &quot;<i>character-as-fate</i>.&quot; To steal once again from XKCD, Beast is a game about how the thing standing in the way of your dreams is that the one having them is you. Beast is a game where you have made peace with the fact that you are a monster, and what you're going to do to defy the obvious thing we do to monsters.<br /> <br /> So, as it relates to the larger context of the conversation, why would anyone want to alleviate the demands Hunger places on their title characters? Deciding what you're going to do with your Hunger, if you're going to try and find a way to be productive and of benefit to your community-if you can dare to dream that's even possible-perhaps taking it too far in one way and creating a draconian slice of reality that &quot;acts on their best behavior&quot; under your violent present, or taking it the other way and abandoning concern for others and serving yourself up a healthy slice of whatever-the-fuck-you-want and relying on being able swat away any challenger-that struggle is already hella strong with Hunger as is. Weakening Hunger diminishes it-the weaker the Hunger is, the less you owe to yourself in defining who you are in relationship to your community.<br /> <br /> That there are some people who refuse to see anyway that Beasts can be a part of their community, healthy, supportive, and productive even-well, Heroes aren't the good guys for a reason.<br /> <br /> The most hilarious part of Beast is honestly the parallels between <i>that</i> text and the many people who think they can fix Beast with their hatred of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, while Beast is not so gauche as to outright say it, it's also funny how many people don't pick up that most Beasts <i>aren't </i>supposed to ultimately succeed. Things to be clear about in the storytelling chapter of the now absolutely-never-going-to-happen Second Edition of Beast, thanks Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-28-2023, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T19:11:53-07:00","id":1524669,"title":"","content":"One thought I had in passing is making beasts pseudo kindred. It is established in Requiem that the different clans started out fairly different from what they are now and they shifted over time to become more alike. What if we just take that and applied it to beasts? <br /> <br /> My thoughts is maybe they're a psychic vampire version of the kindred. In order to feed they have to get a human to spend willpower. This could be done in a variety of methods, if the beast arranged something scary or terrible to happen to a mortal it might force the mortal to spend a willpower point, but it could also encourage them and motivate them to spend will power through positive actions, though I suspect that would be harder. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it would work to keep the same 5 theme that runs through CofD, but I also don't think it would be the worst if it was reduced to 3 types of beasts, a physical, a social, and a mental, and maybe mortals spending a willpower on a skill of the beast's prefered tupe counted double. If you wanted to keep 5 families I suppose you could focus them on smaller groups of skills. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bReducing the number of options available to beasts (ie. From 5 families and 5 hungers down to 1 of 3 skill sets) would probably make for a worse beast only game, I don't know that it would necessarily be a problem in a crossover campaign (or for Beast NPCs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:28:34-07:00","id":1524709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1524667#post1524667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've said before, that in the reductive way to think of games way of analogizing them to singular aspects of human life, the same way some people will say Created is a game about childhood and Curse is a game about old age, that Beast would pretty clearly be the game about celebrity, that they are myth and folklore and creepy pasta given flesh, heart and mind, that it's a game about becoming memetic in that way that haunted houses and death turns and hurricanes and earthquakes do, monstrosity gone viral, and I have taken that read so far as to say that my personal theme for Beast on the whole is <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZDXXi19_7iE\" target=\"_blank\">The Monster by Eminem</a>, so no, I wouldn't say it's <i>too</i> forced.<br /> <br /> That said, Beast is, in a game about monsters, is a crossover template, and by way of being able to relate to any and all of the other splats, ended up in a place where it must reflect and contrast them, and has opted for the route of deconstruction, acting as a mirror that strips the circumstances that makes other monsters defensible (