tive and of benefit to your community-if you can dare to dream that's even possible-perhaps taking it too far in one way and creating a draconian slice of reality that &quot;acts on their best behavior&quot; under your violent present, or taking it the other way and abandoning concern for others and serving yourself up a healthy slice of whatever-the-fuck-you-want and relying on being able swat away any challenger-that struggle is already hella strong with Hunger as is. Weakening Hunger diminishes it-the weaker the Hunger is, the less you owe to yourself in defining who you are in relationship to your community.<br /> <br /> That there are some people who refuse to see anyway that Beasts can be a part of their community, healthy, supportive, and productive even-well, Heroes aren't the good guys for a reason.<br /> <br /> The most hilarious part of Beast is honestly the parallels between <i>that</i> text and the many people who think they can fix Beast with their hatred of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, while Beast is not so gauche as to outright say it, it's also funny how many people don't pick up that most Beasts <i>aren't </i>supposed to ultimately succeed. Things to be clear about in the storytelling chapter of the now absolutely-never-going-to-happen Second Edition of Beast, thanks Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was honestly just going to leave this unanswered, but I got lost on something. What is &quot;that&quot; text you are talking about? And change the beast when you hate it? That doesn't even make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T13:31:13-07:00","id":1524710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1524669#post1524669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thought I had in passing is making beasts pseudo kindred. It is established in Requiem that the different clans started out fairly different from what they are now and they shifted over time to become more alike. What if we just take that and applied it to beasts?<br /> <br /> My thoughts is maybe they're a psychic vampire version of the kindred. In order to feed they have to get a human to spend willpower. This could be done in a variety of methods, if the beast arranged something scary or terrible to happen to a mortal it might force the mortal to spend a willpower point, but it could also encourage them and motivate them to spend will power through positive actions, though I suspect that would be harder.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it would work to keep the same 5 theme that runs through CofD, but I also don't think it would be the worst if it was reduced to 3 types of beasts, a physical, a social, and a mental, and maybe mortals spending a willpower on a skill of the beast's prefered tupe counted double. If you wanted to keep 5 families I suppose you could focus them on smaller groups of skills.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bReducing the number of options available to beasts (ie. From 5 families and 5 hungers down to 1 of 3 skill sets) would probably make for a worse beast only game, I don't know that it would necessarily be a problem in a crossover campaign (or for Beast NPCs).</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of makes sense, it's really not a bad idea, but I'm already having trouble separating Beast from vampires in my head for various reasons, so I just think that in part they should have some identity of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T11:04:37-08:00","id":1525461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1524709#post1524709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is &quot;that&quot; text you are talking about? And change the beast when you hate it? That doesn't even make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arc is referencing Heroes, as mentioned in the line preceding &quot;<i>that</i> text.&quot; Heroes as an antagonist category don't believe Beasts can or should exist as they do (even if the worst thing they do is be the focus of a recurring nightmare), often giving stated reasons for feeling this way that have nothing to do with the Begotten's activities or even reality in general, and most of the more prominent proposed &quot;fixes&quot; on this board have come from people with an avowed dislike of the game based on misunderstandings of the game's text and overall aims. She is describing a course of action that does not make sense in parallel with a character type whose actions do not have a consistent and coherent rationale behind it.<br /> <br /> Given appropriate distancing from the inhuman nature of their abilities, to draw analogy to more common fantasy fare, Beasts' assigned cosmological role runs the gamut from bandit king to demon lord, and by the sensibilities of contemporary fiction we tend to look askance at heroes who think bandits should all die for living in the woods and stealing to eat.<br /> <br /> To bring it back around to the topic, having been born under the banner of the Blue Manticore and needing to enact Ruin to at least some small degree to live a fulfilling life on one's own (or lend their aid to another fatefully compatible monster) is an unconscious decision the character makes at the Devouring because the Hunger of their Horror is important to them as much as the fear their Family relates to.<br /> <br /> Horror-mystery setting that the Chronicles of Darkness is, the supernatural power derived from the fear of the unknown and revelatory shock is narratively relevant; feeding outside of Inflicting Nightmares doesn't drain Willpower or even necessarily inflict a breaking point, but the scale of a feeding roll is a combined function of dramatic investment and appropriateness to the Beast's nature and destiny. Hunger isn't about habits, it's about desire, and specifically interpersonal desires where something is gained at the expense of someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:14:06-08:00","id":1525473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1525461#post1525461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc is referencing Heroes, as mentioned in the line preceding &quot;<i>that</i> text.&quot; Heroes as an antagonist category don't believe Beasts can or should exist as they do (even if the worst thing they do is be the focus of a recurring nightmare), often giving stated reasons for feeling this way that have nothing to do with the Begotten's activities or even reality in general, and most of the more prominent proposed &quot;fixes&quot; on this board have come from people with an avowed dislike of the game based on misunderstandings of the game's text and overall aims. She is describing a course of action that does not make sense in parallel with a character type whose actions do not have a consistent and coherent rationale behind it.<br /> <br /> Given appropriate distancing from the inhuman nature of their abilities, to draw analogy to more common fantasy fare, Beasts' assigned cosmological role runs the gamut from bandit king to demon lord, and by the sensibilities of contemporary fiction we tend to look askance at heroes who think bandits should all die for living in the woods and stealing to eat.<br /> <br /> To bring it back around to the topic, having been born under the banner of the Blue Manticore and needing to enact Ruin to at least some small degree to live a fulfilling life on one's own (or lend their aid to another fatefully compatible monster) is an unconscious decision the character makes at the Devouring because the Hunger of their Horror is important to them as much as the fear their Family relates to.<br /> <br /> Horror-mystery setting that the Chronicles of Darkness is, the supernatural power derived from the fear of the unknown and revelatory shock is narratively relevant; feeding outside of Inflicting Nightmares doesn't drain Willpower or even necessarily inflict a breaking point, but the scale of a feeding roll is a combined function of dramatic investment and appropriateness to the Beast's nature and destiny. Hunger isn't about habits, it's about desire, and specifically interpersonal desires where something is gained at the expense of someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok... but your intention with the last two paragraphs was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:58:13-08:00","id":1525481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1523526-hunger-with-changes?p=1525473#post1525473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok... but your intention with the last two paragraphs was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pointing out that making Hunger about habits rather than about fear doesn't track (the scale works the way that it does because some characters will maintain their Satiety through habit and others will maintain it through periodic grand gestures), that a character's Horror is as much a totemic icon of their Hunger (e.g. enacting Ruin under the banner of the Blue Manticore) as it is a literal monstrous form with which to exert supernatural power, that e.g. making feeding the Hunger for Punishment scale with the crime rather than the punishment makes for a dissatisfying outcome if High Satiety feeding can be accomplished by saying &quot;boo&quot; to a billionaire, and that a character's Hunger is generally for something that they want on some level (to the point where satiation is easier if it aligns with their Aspirations) in a fashion that stirs the interpersonal soul but does not necessarily have any game-mechanical impact on the target's well-being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}